I come inside the big metro station.
This station is very clean and big.
I go near the ticket counter.
There is a man behind the counter.
"Hello sir," I say.
"Hello madam," he says.
"Where do you need to go?" he asks.
"I need to get to the station near the sea," I explain.
"Do you want a ticket?" he asks.
"No, I want a permanent metro card," I say.
"Okay madam, it costs one hundred rupees for this," he says.
I take out money from my bag.
I give him one hundred rupees.
He gives me a new metro card.
I say thank you to him.
I put my card in the bag.
Now I need to board the metro.
I go towards the platform.
